-- title:
--   Transport of descent intertwining data along a tower isomorphism
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $q,q',r$, indices $ir,irbar \in \mathrm{Fin}\,2$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose decomposition group over $\mathbb Q$ acts isometrically (together with decidability of equality on the completion $A.valuation.Completion$). Fix $a,b \in \mathbb Q$, a homomorphism $\rho$ from the units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ to $\mathrm{PGL}(2)$ over the closure of $\mathbb Q$ inside the completion, a pseudo-uniformizer $\varpi$ for that pair (an element of the base field whose valuation in the completion lies strictly between $0$ and $1$ and is cofinal in both directions), with $\mathrm{Omega.HolRingOf}\ \varpi\ \rho$ — the ring of functions on the $p$-adic upper half-plane holomorphic on every affinoid — assumed a domain. Fix level subgroups $\Gamma_j$ indexed by $\mathrm{HeckeTower.Obj}\ q\ q' = \mathrm{Option}$ of the primes away from $q,q'$, quaternion units $w_j,\bar w_j$ and $s_\ell$, a homomorphism $dIso$ from the decomposition subgroup to isometric automorphisms of the completion fixing the base, a base field $F_0$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with decomposition-group semilinear action $gal_0$ and semilinear involutive data $W : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to$ semilinear automorphisms, and a character $\chi$ to $\mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb Z/2)$. Let $\mathbb T, \mathbb T'$ be two sets of tower data over $F_0$ (for each prime $\ell$ away from $q,q'$ a field $F_\ell$ which is a curve over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, together with two degeneracy $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra embeddings $\varphi_{\ell,i} : F_0 \to F_\ell$, finite and integral), with arbitrary upper-level data $galT, WT$ for $\mathbb T$ and $galT', WT'$ for $\mathbb T'$. Assume $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra isomorphisms $\theta_\ell : \mathbb T.F\,\ell \to \mathbb T'.F\,\ell$ compatible with both degeneracy maps, $\theta_{\ell}(\mathbb T.\varphi_{(\ell,i)} x) = \mathbb T'.\varphi_{(\ell,i)} x$ for all $x \in F_0$, and ring homomorphisms $\iota_j, \iota'_j$ from the $j$-th field of $\mathbb T$, resp. $\mathbb T'$, into $\mathrm{FractionRing}(\mathrm{Omega.HolRingOf}\ \varpi\ \rho)$ such that $\iota_{\mathrm{none}} = \iota'_{\mathrm{none}}$ on $F_0$ and $\iota_{\mathrm{some}\,\ell} = \iota'_{\mathrm{some}\,\ell} \circ \theta_\ell$. Then $\mathrm{DescentIntertwiningBase}$ for the primed data implies it for the unprimed data. The predicate is the conjunction of: $\chi$ trivial on inertia at $A$; $\chi$ nontrivial on any Frobenius at $A$ of level $r$; $\chi\tau = 1$ exactly when $\tau$ fixes every element of the residue field of $A$ satisfying $x^{r^2} = x$; the compatibility of $\iota_{\mathrm{none}}$ on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with the structural map from the completion; the statement that the subfield generated by the image of the completion together with the image of $\iota_{\mathrm{none}}$ is the $\Gamma_{\mathrm{none}}$-invariant field $\mathrm{Mumford.invariantFieldOf}$; preservation of linear independence of finite subsets of the base level from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to the completion; and further clauses, summarised here, expressing the behaviour of $\iota_{\mathrm{none}}$ under the decomposition group via $gal_0$, $dIso$, $\chi$ and under $W$, and two degeneracy clauses relating $\iota_{\mathrm{some}\,\ell} \circ \varphi_{(\ell,0)}$ and $\iota_{\mathrm{some}\,\ell} \circ \varphi_{(\ell,1)}$ to $\iota_{\mathrm{none}}$. No compatibility between $galT, WT$ and $galT', WT'$ is required.
--
--   This is a transport statement for the base-level part of the Čerednik–Drinfeld descent datum: an isomorphism of prime-to-$qq'$ Hecke tower data over a fixed base field, compatible with both degeneracy embeddings, carries the datum from one tower to the other. It is used by the two existence results for such base data coming from a rigid oriented moduli witness, which need the datum for a tower presented in a different but isomorphic form.
